# Global UX Rules

Every flow should satisfy:

Maximum three navigation levels.

Maximum two taps for common tasks.

Never lose user progress.

Never display technical jargon.

Always offer recovery.

Always preserve context.

---

# Error Recovery Principles

When something fails:

Explain what happened.

Explain why.

Suggest the next step.

Offer Retry.

Never leave the user at a dead end.

---

# Success Metrics

95% of users complete onboarding without assistance.

90% of users discover devices automatically.

80% of users create their first Scene within five minutes.

Common tasks require two taps or fewer.

Recovery flows succeed without external documentation.

---

# User Flow Principles

The best user flow is the one users never notice.

If users must think about navigation, the flow should be redesigned.

